      "Hatteker's pitch is simple: **more attachment heads than anything else in this price range**, all waterproof, all charged over a standard USB-C cable instead of a proprietary dock. The **LED runtime display** is a genuinely useful touch that's missing even on shavers twice the price — you get an exact readout instead of guessing whether you have enough juice left for a full session.",
      "The **90-minute runtime** on paper is the longest of any battery-powered shaver here, but that number is somewhat inflated by the lower-torque motor sipping less power per minute. On our thick-hair stall test, the Hatteker needed the most passes of any waterproof unit to fully clear a dense patch — it never stalled outright, but you'll move slower than with the Mangroomer or Panasonic. For regular maintenance shaving rather than clearing months of neglected growth, that's a non-issue. The **sliding plastic back extension arm** clicks the main unit into a 16-inch reach, which covers most men adequately, though the plastic housing doesn't feel as rugged as the metal-reinforced arms on pricier units.",
    ],
