      "Attachment Heads": "Curved wide blade + 12-inch extension handle",
      "Charging Method": "Proprietary charging base",
    },
    bottomLine:
      "The fastest way to clear a large back. The curved 2.5-inch blade covers so much ground per pass that the shorter battery life rarely matters in practice.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "Remington's back variant of the Shortcut Pro wins on **blade geometry, not battery specs**. The nearly **2.5-inch curved stainless blade** is the widest cutting surface of any electric shaver in this roundup, which means it simply requires fewer passes to clear the same area. During testing, sessions with the Shortcut Pro were consistently the **shortest in total time**, even though its 40-minute battery runtime is the lowest number on paper.",
      "The motor itself held up well under load — Remington doesn't advertise a torque figure, but the sustained cutting power through thick patches stayed consistent right up until the battery indicator dropped low, unlike some competitors that visibly slow down in the final 10 minutes of charge. It is **washable under running water for cleanup**, but Remington does not rate it for submersion or shower use, so treat it as a dry-or-rinse-only tool. The **12-inch extension handle** is shorter than most dedicated back shavers, but the blade width compensates by covering more surface area per stroke.",
    ],
  },
  {
    id: "panasonic-er-gk60",
    name: "Panasonic ER-GK60 Body Groomer",
    category: "Electric Body Groomer (Battery)",
    price: 39.99,
    rating: 4.6,
    reviewCount: 5800,
    badge: "Best Battery Life",
    bestFor: "Long Sessions, Wet/Dry Flexibility",
    amazonUrl: "#",
    pros: [
      "IPX7 waterproof — safe for shower use, wet or dry shaving",
      "Dual-edge blade design cuts on both forward and backward strokes",
      "Five comb attachments for precise length control (0.5mm to 20mm)",
      "Consistent torque throughout the entire charge cycle",
      "Compact, travel-friendly form factor",
    ],
    cons: [
      "No dedicated back extension arm included — needs a paired handle for full reach",
      "Charging indicator is a single LED, not a percentage display",
    ],
    specs: {
      "Battery Type": "Lithium-ion (built-in, rechargeable)",
      "Runtime": "50 min continuous use",
      "Charge Time": "~1 hour to full (8 min quick-charge = 5 min runtime)",
      "Waterproof Rating": "IPX7 (fully submersible, shower-safe)",
      "Motor / Torque": "Linear motor with stable torque curve",
      "Attachment Heads": "Dual-edge blade + 5 length combs (0.5mm-20mm)",
      "Charging Method": "Proprietary charging cradle with quick-charge",
    },
    bottomLine:
      "A Japanese-engineered motor that doesn't lose steam as the battery drains. Best paired with an extension grip for full back coverage, but unmatched consistency stroke to stroke.",
    descriptionParagraphs: [
      "Panasonic doesn't market the ER-GK60 as a dedicated back shaver, but its **dual-edge cutting blade** and **linear motor** make it one of the most technically impressive battery-powered groomers we tested for back hair once paired with a third-party extension handle. Unlike shavers that visibly lose torque as the charge depletes, the ER-GK60's motor held a **flat, stable torque curve** from full charge down to low battery — a detail that matters more than peak power for a tool you're using in a single 10-15 minute session.",
      "The **five interchangeable combs** (0.5mm to 20mm) give more granular length control than any other electric shaver in this guide, which is genuinely useful for men who want to gradually reduce back hair length over several sessions rather than going straight to skin. It's rated **IPX7 waterproof**, so shower use and wet shaving are both fully supported, and an **8-minute quick-charge** yields roughly 5 minutes of runtime — enough to rescue a session if you forgot to charge overnight. The one real limitation: Panasonic sells this as a general body groomer, not a back-specific tool, so out of the box it lacks the long extension arm that dedicated back shavers include.",
    ],
